-- title:
--   Igusa-branch prolongation at a node, with rational branch place
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`, and for a valuation subring the associated residue field and maximal ideal are written in the usual way. The field `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` is the intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$ generated by the coefficientwise images of the elements of `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, the latter being generated over $\mathbb Q$ by the series $q$-expansions $\mathrm{qExpand}\,d\,j_q$ for $d\mid M'$; the field `fieldBar q M'` is the corresponding base change of the function field `xHFunctionField (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$, i.e. the subgroup of units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$. The field `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` is the intermediate field of $\kappa\subseteq\kappa((T))$ generated by `jqModC κ` and `jqNModC κ M'`. A `Place K F` is a valuation subring of $F$ containing the image of $K$, different from $F$, whose ideals are principal; `ord` is minus the logarithm of its adic valuation, `IsRational` says that $K$ surjects onto its residue field, and `evalAt` sends an element of the valuation subring to the constant in $K$ representing its residue (and other elements to $0$). A `ConstantReduction A F Fbar` consists of a valuation subring `integers` of $F$ contracting to $A$ on constants, a surjective ring homomorphism `residue` to `Fbar` with kernel the maximal ideal of `integers`, compatible with reduction of constants, a scaling clause making every nonzero element of $F$ a constant multiple of one with nonzero residue, and a map `placeMap` on places preserving degrees and compatible with divisors of elements of nonzero residue; a `RegularProlongation A F Fbar` is the same data without `placeMap` and the two clauses concerning it.
--
--   Data fixed at the outset. A prime $q$, a nonzero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, a valuation subring $A\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $q$ a nonunit of $A$ (the hypothesis `hA`), and $\kappa=\mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$. A finite set $W$ of places of `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` over $\kappa$ which, by `hW`, consists exactly of the supersingular places, i.e. those $w$ that are rational, are affine geometric places in the sense of `IsAffineGeomPlace`, and satisfy $w.\mathrm{evalAt}(\mathrm{jGeomGen}\,\kappa\,M')\in\mathrm{ssJSet}\,q\,\kappa$; and an element $s\in W$. The hypothesis `hle` is the inclusion `modularFunctionFieldBar M' ≤ fieldBar q M'`. A constant reduction $R_0$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $A$ with values in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'`, subject to two further hypotheses: `hR₀`, that for every Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$ whose coefficientwise image in $\overline{\mathbb Q}((T))$ lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, that image is $R_0$-integral and its $R_0$-residue, viewed as a Laurent series over $\kappa$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and `hGU`, the rigidity clause asserting that a valuation subring $V$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` has the same elements as $R_0$`.integers` as soon as $V$ contracts to $A$ on constants, contains the coefficientwise image of $j_q$, and has the residual-transcendence property that whenever a polynomial $p$ over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with all coefficients in $A$ has $p$ evaluated at that image of $j_q$ in the maximal ideal of $V$, all coefficients of $p$ lie in the maximal ideal of $V$.
--
--   The constant-field data. An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$, such that $A\cap k_0$ (formally, the contraction of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$) is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`) with maximal ideal generated by $\pi_0$ (`hunif`), is henselian (`hhens`), and has algebraically closed residue field (`hres`); and `hκ`, that every $a\in A$ is congruent modulo the maximal ideal of $A$ to some $c\in k_0$ lying in $A$. The conclusion is stated for the $k_0$-algebra structure on `fieldBar q M'` obtained by composing $k_0\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\to$ `fieldBar q M'`.
--
--   The level field and the supersingular valuation ring. For every intermediate field $F_0$ of $k_0\subseteq$ `fieldBar q M'` such that (i) the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ is all of `fieldBar q M'`, and (ii) $F_0$ is linearly disjoint from the constants in the following sense: for every intermediate field $K'$ of $k_0\subseteq\overline{\mathbb Q}$ finite over $k_0$, every $m$, every $c:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ and every $a:\mathrm{Fin}\,m\to$ `fieldBar q M'` whose values lie in the compositum of $F_0$ with the $k_0$-subfield generated by the image of $K'$, the relation $\sum_i c_i\,a_i=0$ forces $a_i=0$ for all $i$. For every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ which contracts to $A$ on $k_0$, is a discrete valuation ring, and has maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$.
--
--   The node. For every subring $O$ of $F_0$, local and Noetherian, such that $O\subseteq W_0$; $O$ contracts to $A$ on $k_0$; every $f\in O$ admits $x\in k_0$ with $x\in A$, with image in $O$, and with $f-x$ a nonunit of $O$; and every $f\in F_0$ satisfies $f\,h=g$ for some $g,h\in O$ with $h\neq0$. For every $E_0\geq1$, every $c_x,c_y\in O$, every unit $u$ of $O$, every ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the adic completion of $O$ at its maximal ideal onto the crossing model `UVCrossingModel` over the adic completion $\widehat{A\cap k_0}$ with parameter the $E_0$-th power of the image of $\pi_0$, that is $\widehat{A\cap k_0}[[X_0,X_1]]/(X_0X_1-\pi_0^{E_0})$, and all units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$ of that model, subject to: $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$ in $O$; $\iota$ sends the image in the completion of a constant $x\in k_0\cap A$ lying in $O$ to `UVCrossingModel.const` of the image of $x$; $\iota$ sends the image of $c_x$ to $\gamma_U\cdot$`UVCrossingModel.U` and the image of $c_y$ to $\gamma_V\cdot$`UVCrossingModel.V`; and $c_y\in W_0$ with $c_y$ in the maximal ideal of $W_0$, while $c_x$, if it lies in $W_0$, is not in the maximal ideal of $W_0$.
--
--   The Igusa branch. For every valuation subring $W_x$ of $F_0$ such that $O\subseteq W_x$; $W_x$ contracts to $A$ on $k_0$; $W_x$ is a discrete valuation ring with maximal ideal generated by the image of $\pi_0$; there exists $t\in W_x$ with the residual-transcendence property that whenever a polynomial $p$ over $k_0$ all of whose coefficients lie in $A$ has $p$ evaluated at $t$ in the maximal ideal of $W_x$, all coefficients of $p$ lie in the maximal ideal of $W_x$; $c_x$ lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ and $c_y$ does not; and, finally, the level-$M'$ reading laws: for every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'` whose coefficientwise image is $R_0$-integral (witness `hgi`) and which is regular wherever $j$ is, in the sense that every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ with $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $j_q$ nonnegative also has $P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of $g$ nonnegative, the image of $g$ in `fieldBar q M'` lies in $F_0$ and, as an element of $F_0$, lies in $W_x$; it lies in the maximal ideal of $W_x$ if and only if its $R_0$-residue vanishes; and if its $R_0$-residue lies in the valuation subring of $s$, then it lies in $O$, and for every $c\in k_0\cap A$ with image in $O$ whose residue in $\kappa$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}$ of that $R_0$-residue, the difference of the two elements of $O$ is not a unit of $O$.
--
--   Lastly, a field $FSS$ over $\kappa$ and a regular prolongation $R$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in $FSS$ whose integers cut out $W_0$ on $F_0$, i.e. for $f\in F_0$ one has $f\in R$`.integers` if and only if $f\in W_0$.
--
--   Conclusion. There exist a field $FI$ over $\kappa$, a regular prolongation $R_x$ of $A$ on `fieldBar q M'` with values in $FI$, and a place $b_x$ of $FI$ over $\kappa$ such that:
--
--   (1) $R_x$ cuts out $W_x$ on $F_0$: for $f\in F_0$, $f\in R_x$`.integers` if and only if $f\in W_x$;
--
--   (2) $b_x$ is rational, i.e. $\kappa$ surjects onto its residue field;
--
--   (3) for every $f\in F_0$ lying in $O$ and $R_x$-integral, the $R_x$-residue of $f$ lies in the valuation subring of $b_x$;
--
--   (4) for every such $f$ which is moreover a nonunit of $O$, the $R_x$-residue of $f$ lies in the maximal ideal of the valuation subring of $b_x$;
--
--   (5) $b_x$ is the unique place of $FI$ over $\kappa$ with properties (3) and (4): any place $y$ of $FI$ over $\kappa$ whose valuation subring contains the $R_x$-residues of the $R_x$-integral elements of $O$ and in whose maximal ideal lie the $R_x$-residues of the $R_x$-integral nonunits of $O$ equals $b_x$;
--
--   (6) if $c_x$ is $R_x$-integral, then its $R_x$-residue is $0$;
--
--   (7) if $c_y$ is $R_x$-integral, then $b_x.\mathrm{ord}$ of its $R_x$-residue equals $1$;
--
--   (8) every $R_0$-integral element of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` has image in `fieldBar q M'` lying in $R_x$`.integers`;
--
--   (9) there is a ring homomorphism $j:$ `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` $\to FI$ such that for every $R_0$-integral $f$ the image of $f$ in `fieldBar q M'` is $R_x$-integral with $R_x$-residue $j$ applied to the $R_0$-residue of $f$, and such that for every $g$ in `modularFunctionFieldC κ M'` one has $g$ in the valuation subring of $s$ if and only if $j(g)$ lies in the valuation subring of $b_x$.
--
--   This is the Igusa-side half of the local analysis at one node of the semistable model of the modular curve of level $q^2M'$ attached to the units congruent to $1$ modulo $q$: starting from a crossing presentation $\widehat{O}\cong\widehat{A\cap k_0}[[U,V]]/(UV-\pi_0^{E_0})$ of the node and from the branch valuation ring $W_x$ along which the Igusa component runs, it produces a regular prolongation $R_x$ realising $W_x$, together with the rational branch place $b_x$ of the residue field at which the node sits, the two coordinate laws ($c_x$ reducing to $0$, $c_y$ of order one at $b_x$), integrality of the level-$M'$ functions and the identification of $b_x$ with the chosen supersingular place $s$ through an embedding of the level-$M'$ function field over $\kappa$. It is used by the two statements assembling node centres and layered node rings for the Igusa separation at level $q^2M'$.
